   "source": [
    "## 1. Bubble Sort - Simple but Slow\n",
    "\n",
    "**What it is:**\n",
    "Repeatedly step through the list, compare adjacent elements, and swap them if they're in the wrong order. Smaller elements \"bubble\" toward the beginning.\n",
    "\n",
    "**How it works:**\n",
    "1. Start at the beginning of the list\n",
    "2. Compare each pair of adjacent elements\n",
    "3. If the left one is bigger than the right one, swap them\n",
    "4. Move to the next pair\n",
    "5. Repeat until a full pass makes no swaps (list is sorted)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Example: Sorting [5, 2, 8, 1]**\n",
    "```\n",
    "Pass 1: [5,2,8,1] → [2,5,8,1] → [2,5,1,8]\n",
    "Pass 2: [2,5,1,8] → [2,1,5,8]\n",
    "Pass 3: [2,1,5,8] → [1,2,5,8] ✓ Sorted!\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Time Complexity:**\n",
    "- Best: O(n) if already sorted (with optimization)\n",
    "- Average: O(n²)\n",
    "- Worst: O(n²)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why learn it:**\n",
    "- Understand basic sorting logic\n",
    "- Example of a simple but inefficient algorithm\n",
    "- Foundation for understanding other sorts\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why it matters for LLMs:**\n",
    "- Ordering results by relevance/priority\n",
    "- Sorting when performance isn't critical\n",
    "\n",
    "**Requirements:**\n",
    "- Sort an array of integers in ascending order\n",
    "- Handle empty arrays and single elements\n",
    "- Implement the basic algorithm (not optimized yet)"
   ]
  },
