    "## 3. Insertion Sort - Build as You Go\n",
    "\n",
    "**What it is:**\n",
    "Build a sorted array one element at a time. Take each element from the unsorted part and insert it into the correct position in the sorted part.\n",
    "\n",
    "**How it works:**\n",
    "1. Start with first element (it's sorted by itself)\n",
    "2. Take the next element\n",
    "3. Shift all larger sorted elements to the right\n",
    "4. Insert the new element in its correct position\n",
    "5. Repeat for all elements\n",
    "\n",
    "**Example: Sorting [5, 2, 8, 1, 9]**\n",
    "```\n",
    "Start: [5] (sorted part)\n",
    "Insert 2: [2, 5]\n",
    "Insert 8: [2, 5, 8]\n",
    "Insert 1: [1, 2, 5, 8]\n",
    "Insert 9: [1, 2, 5, 8, 9] ✓\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Time Complexity:**\n",
    "- Best: O(n) if already sorted\n",
    "- Average: O(n²)\n",
    "- Worst: O(n²)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why it matters for LLMs:**\n",
    "- **Online algorithm**: Works while data arrives (doesn't need full array upfront)\n",
    "- Fast on nearly-sorted data\n",
    "- Used in many practical systems for real-world data\n",
    "\n",
    "**Requirements:**\n",
    "- Sort array in ascending order\n",
    "- Work on partially sorted data efficiently\n",
    "- Handle empty arrays and single elements"
   ]
